--- !u!114 &818513539
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 818513537}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "On the floating isle of Luma-5, every young jelly learned to glow by the
    end of their first year. The glow was a sign of joy, a pulsing light that showed
    they had found their inner warmth. But one jelly, named Gloop, never glowed at
    all, no matter how hard he laughed or danced.\nHe tried everything \u2014 starfruit
    candy, upside-down bouncing, even being tickled by feather-worms. The other jellies
    watched, curious and concerned, as he remained dull in a world of shimmer. At
    first, they encouraged him with patience. Then came the whispers.\nGloop, hurt
    but determined, left the village to seek his glow in the far reaches of the isles.
    He wandered into a cave of storm-stones, a place feared by most for its unpredictable
    flashes and rumbles. But Gloop wasn\u2019t afraid of darkness. He simply wanted
    to understand why he didn\u2019t shine.\nInside the cave, he found a creature
    no one had seen in generations \u2014 a trembling larva that had lost its nest
    during a quake. Its eyes blinked slowly, barely visible. Gloop didn\u2019t hesitate.
    He wrapped his jelly body around the small being and sang the only lullaby he
    knew, his voice soft and unsure.\nA golden shimmer rose from within him \u2014
    not bright, not flashy, but steady and warm. It lit the cave just enough to calm
    the creature, who curled into his side with a sigh. Gloop stared at the light,
    wide-eyed. For the first time, he was glowing.\nWhen he returned to the village,
    he wasn\u2019t met with gasps or applause \u2014 just quiet wonder. He didn\u2019t
    sparkle during dances or flash when he giggled, but his glow appeared when it
    mattered: when someone was sad, scared, or in need of comfort.\nGloop became
    known not for his brightness, but for his timing. He was the jelly that lit up
    the darkest corners, not the brightest skies. And slowly, even the most radiant
    jellies wished they could glow like him \u2014 from within, and with purpose.\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 84a1fe4eefd208f43b95cd1493db4bb3, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2605340879131967097, guid: 84a1fe4eefd208f43b95cd1493db4bb3, type: 2}
