MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1889967313}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7fe4e4d5e6f7d4c4a90309ddff04610b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _view: {fileID: 2073268566}
  _screenType: 4
  isActive: 0
  storyImage: {fileID: 210358982}
  title: {fileID: 276468571}
  description: {fileID: 818513539}
  close: {fileID: 1276699867}
  _stories:
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a32d360898c438e40ba1db2b9e6618f3, type: 3}
    title: The Hologel That Dreamed in Spectrum
    description: "High on the marble terraces of Olympus, where sunrise gilded ancient
      columns, every Hologel glowed in one fixed hue\u2014emerald by dawn, sapphire
      by noon, violet by dusk. Tradition held that these colors were gifts from the
      mountain\u2019s heart and never changed. But one curious creature named Neon
      felt confined by a single tint. Each morning, while mist curled around apses
      and moss-edged steps, Neon closed its eyes and pictured ribbons of every color
      spiraling through its core: ruby red, citrine yellow, coral pink, and every
      shade between.\r\nBy day, he practiced coaxing flashes of new light. He poured
      himself into tiny bursts of sunset orange, only to watch the glow crackle and
      collapse into dull patches. The other Hologels paused their quiet promenades
      across the terraces to observe his erratic \u201Cpatchwork\u201D efforts, murmuring
      among themselves as Neon\u2019s radiance stuttered like a broken prism. Determined,
      he ventured beyond the temple walls, slipping past ivy-clad buttresses to reach
      the fabled Opal Caverns, carved deep into Olympus\u2019s northern flank.\r\nInside
      those twisting tunnels, walls studded with crystal veins caught stray beams
      and refracted them into kaleidoscopes. Neon followed the scattered rainbows
      through echoing halls until at last he found the Prism Heart\u2014a massive
      gemstone hovering above a subterranean pool. Its facets shivered with every
      conceivable shade, from moonlit silver to twilight indigo. With a steady thrum
      of will, Neon wove his single-hued glow into the gem\u2019s living spectrum.
      The cavern erupted in a burst of prismatic light so vibrant the very quartz
      sang in response.\r\nWhen Neon reappeared on the sunlit terraces, he did not
      hold one hue but pulsed through rainbows with every heartbeat. Other Hologels
      gathered in awe as Neon traced luminous arcs across the sky. Under the hush
      of carved archways and within the breath of dawn winds, they learned that true
      wonder comes not from a single gift, but from daring to dream in every color.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0d8d9b66ba6ab714382cbf62237775d2, type: 3}
    title: The Lost Echo of the Summit Canyon
    description: "Atop Olympus\u2019s wind-scarred summit lay the Summit Canyon,
      a yawning rift whose sheer walls of white marble rose like silent sentinels.
      Explorers sent echo-probes into its depths, yet every probe returned only empty
      silence. Scholars declared the canyon a \u201Cdead zone,\u201D while merchants
      warned caravans to avoid its edge. Captain Miri, drawn by curiosity rather
      than creed, would not accept that blankness defined the chasm.\r\nShe tethered
      her wind-glider to a weathered pillar at dawn\u2019s first light and descended
      along the canyon\u2019s rim. Below her boots, the marble hummed faintly, as
      though the mountain itself reserved a secret. Drawn by that tremor, she found
      a narrow fissure leading into a hidden grotto, where emerald lichen glowed
      like embers on pale stone. Suspended above a shallow pool floated a sphere
      of translucent ether, its surface quivering with imperceptible pulses.\r\nMiri
      pressed her palm to the orb. Immediately, the cavern erupted in sound: harmonies
      of distant waterfalls, low thunder that spoke of ancient avalanches, and whispered
      breezes carrying secrets of frost-tipped ridges. The lost echoes of Olympus
      poured forth, telling of days when the mountain rang with ritual drums and
      jubilant song. As the resonance subsided, Captain Miri realized she held more
      than data\u2014she held the mountain\u2019s own memories.\r\nWord spread across
      the temples and spire-topped villages. Pilgrims journeyed to the canyon\u2019s
      overlook to feel the lingering hum beneath their feet. Poets composed verses
      in the grotto\u2019s reverb, while musicians tuned lyres to the cavern\u2019s
      chord. Miri became known not for conquest, but for listening where others heard
      only silence\u2014reminding all who climbed Olympus that deeper than any stone
      lies the voice of memory, waiting to be heard.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f06f7c93e5c62e145a93ce6822ef5a5b, type: 3}
    title: Maro and the Luminous Vine
    description: "On a terraced garden carved into the western slope of Olympus,
      delicate vines draped over moss-edged fountains of polished marble. Maro, a
      gentle caretaker with fur tinted like dawn mist, spoke softly to each plant,
      coaxing petals to unfurl in pastel glow. One evening, beneath lanterns shaped
      from moonstone, he discovered an unusual vine\u2014its tendril ashen and brittle,
      devoid of the customary shimmer.\r\nConcerned, Maro carried the vine through
      arched colonnades to a hidden grotto lit by phosphorescent mushrooms. He sang
      lullabies in the cavern\u2019s hush and watered its roots with drops drawn
      from the fountain\u2019s pure spring. Yet daybreak found the vine still dull,
      its veins empty of light. Undeterred, Maro scoured the temple\u2019s storerooms
      and found an ancient flask of distilled starlight\u2014rumored to hold celestial
      energy from the mountain\u2019s birth.\r\nAt twilight, he poured the shimmering
      liquid along the vine\u2019s length. Hour by hour, faint pulses blossomed at
      each node: first a whisper of lavender, then a glow of golden rose. By midnight,
      the vine had transformed into a living corridor of luminescence, winding through
      the grotto like a tunnel of soft fireworks. At its farthest arch, Maro discovered
      a hidden alcove where liquid starlight pooled\u2014its surface rippling with
      visions of the mountain\u2019s distant past.\r\nAs Maro sipped from the pool,
      he experienced flashes of long-forgotten celebrations: dancers swirling beneath
      constellations, chanting echoing through vaulted halls, and vows exchanged
      under the first light of dawn. Each memory bound him more deeply to Olympus\u2019s
      spirit. From then on, Maro tended the Luminous Vine nightly, guiding travelers
      along its glowing path. Pilgrims emerged from the grotto with tears and laughter,
      carrying relics of ancient joy in their hearts. In Maro\u2019s gentle hands,
      a single dull tendril had become a living beacon\u2014proof that even the faintest
      spark can kindle the brightest legacy.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: df797e9e9ed31174b9ec3c8bae652038, type: 3}
    title: "The Wanderer\u2019s Prism"
    description: "Beyond the cloud-shrouded peaks of Olympus, traders and wanderers
      traversed precarious ridges in search of rare artifacts. One such traveler,
      Elyx, carried a pouch of glittering curiosities collected from distant lands\u2014moon-tinted
      fossils, fragments of sky-glass, and vials of star-dust. At a dusk-lit bazaar
      perched on a crumbling terrace, a cloaked merchant offered him a small, chipped
      prism rumored to hold \u201Clost reflections.\u201D Intrigued by its weight
      and the faint melody echoing from its fractured facets, Elyx slipped the prism
      into his satchel and continued his journey toward the summit.\r\nThat night,
      under a canopy of swirling auroras, the prism pulsed and projected ghostly
      images onto the terrace\u2019s marble floor: children playing beneath apple
      blossom boughs, laughter rising like bubbles from a hidden spring, and whispered
      conversations beneath lantern-lit arches. Elyx realized the prism held more
      than light\u2014it held memories longing to be released.\r\nAt dawn, he climbed
      to an ancient observatory carved into the cliffs, where the aged caretaker
      Hayan lived in solitude. Presenting the prism, Elyx watched as Hayan\u2019s
      weathered fingers trembled. When the prism touched his palm, it shattered open
      like a delicate flower, releasing streams of colored motes that danced upward
      before dissolving into sunlight. In that moment, Hayan\u2019s eyes shone with
      remembered joy: feasts shared in candlelit halls, songs that echoed through
      marble corridors, and promises whispered beneath starlit skies.\r\nWord spread
      that Elyx had freed lost reflections. He became known not as a peddler, but
      as a healer of echoes. From that day on, he traveled Olympus\u2019s winding
      paths offering weary souls the chance to glimpse\u2014and reclaim\u2014the
      fragments of their own untold stories.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b4e97e479b86c4a438c73a3e3422e827, type: 3}
    title: The Starlight Cartographer
    description: "Lyne\u2019s workshop overlooked the sprawling cloud-cities clinging
      to Olympus\u2019s slopes. By day, she charted the luminous air-currents that
      wove between towers of alabaster and sapphire. Her star-maps, inked in glow-dust,
      guided wind-sailors on safe passage through flickering storms. Yet blank spaces
      bothered her\u2014the dark patches where no current dared to stray.\r\nGuided
      by restless curiosity, Lyne launched in her crystal skiff at twilight, oars
      humming on silken air. She drifted beyond the city\u2019s spires into silent
      realms where stars seemed to hang motionless. For nights she searched, instruments
      spinning, until at last her hull brushed a drifting shard of living mirage.
      Compelled, she dipped her oar into its liquid shimmer. Instantly, invisible
      currents rippled into sight\u2014silver ribbons of wind that arced around hidden
      islets and murmured secrets of the mountain\u2019s secret breath.\r\nReturning
      triumphant, Lyne unfurled her updated charts before the Council of Navigators.
      She traced arcs of light across once-empty skies, linking floating watchtowers
      and crystal-tipped pylons. Merchants re-routed caravans to harness these newfound
      streams, while explorers designed new wind-ships to surf their arcs like cosmic
      sea foam.\r\nCelebrated as the Starlight Cartographer, Lyne remained drawn
      to the horizon. Each dawn saw her launch again, guided by the conviction that
      even the darkest voids can glow if one only dips an oar into the unknown.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 60e88a7ead20bf741a8239bbe96bca39, type: 3}
    title: "Zephyr\u2019s Silent Choir"
    description: "At the edge of Olympus\u2019s highest terrace stood an ancient
      amphitheater of wind-polished marble monoliths. Each dawn, unseen currents
      coursed through the columns, weaving a layered tapestry of sound known as the
      Zephyr\u2019s Choir. Travelers paused on misty steps to listen, claiming the
      breezes carried echoes of long-lost hymns and starlit lullabies. Yet young
      Kiri\u2014born amid the clamor of market squares and bustling courtyards\u2014heard
      nothing but empty air. Determined to join the choir, she apprenticed herself
      to a retired sound-weaver who taught her to sense the subtlest tremors of stone
      and the faintest susurrations of wind.\r\nFor months, Kiri studied ancient
      wind-chant scrolls by candlelight, her finger tracing faded notation that promised
      harmony if only one could coax the breath of Olympus into song. She fashioned
      dozens of reed whistles from moon-bleached reeds harvested on dusk\u2019s first
      light, each tuned to a single note. Night after night, she climbed the marble
      steps as lanterns glowed like captive stars, playing tentative trills that
      drifted into silence. Frustration mounted as her whistles lay mute against
      the vastness of the sky.\r\nOne pre-dawn morning, when the air was still and
      the amphitheater lay shrouded in lavender half-light, Kiri placed a final whistle\u2014crafted
      from heartwood grafted with fragments of wind-fresco\u2014against her lips.
      She inhaled deeply, recalling every rhythm her mentor had taught her, then
      exhaled in one clear, unwavering note: a single pulse of breath that trembled
      like a heartbeat. The amphitheater paused. The marble pillars resonated, awakening
      long-dormant channels carved beneath their bases. One by one, currents of air
      intertwined with Kiri\u2019s note, looping back in rich counterpoint.\r\nThe
      effect was immediate: The Zephyr\u2019s Choir bloomed in breathtaking harmony,
      each monolith contributing its own timbre\u2014a deep undercurrent of rumble,
      a soft harmony of whisper, a crystalline tone that danced above them all. Wind
      eddied around Kiri in gentle vortexes, lifting her hair and swirling her folds
      of cloth as if celebrating her arrival.\r\nNews of her triumph spread like
      wildfire. Merchants closed their stalls at dawn to hear the new chorus. Poets
      penned verses that sought to capture the choir\u2019s layered resonance. Minstrels
      visited, grafting Kiri\u2019s signature note into their ballads. And every
      morning thereafter, Kiri returned to the amphitheater\u2019s center, standing
      alone amid the colonnade, breathing life into the wind with her single, vital
      tone\u2014reminding Olympus that true unity arises not from sameness but from
      the courage to share one\u2019s unique voice.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 446e7f7cc443644419980b82e0ccc181, type: 3}
    title: The Mirror-Staff of the Mountain Artisan
    description: "Deep within a hidden workshop carved into Olympus\u2019s northern
      cliff, artisan Ori shaped wonders from gleaming metal and crystalline shards.
      Her tools whispered of old spells and half-forgotten rites, but her most prized
      possession lay veiled beneath a velvet cloth: a slender silver staff crowned
      with an obsidian mirror, its surface fractured by time yet humming with unseen
      promise. Legend told of an \u201CEcho Gate\u201D sealed within the mountain\u2014a
      threshold to lost knowledge\u2014and Ori believed her mysterious staff might
      unlock it.\r\nOne moonlit night, she studied the mirror\u2019s reflections,
      tilting the staff so that silver light danced across ornate runes etched into
      a hidden door behind stacked crates. A soft pulse throbbed through her fingertips,
      guiding her steps through winding corridors of living rock. Passing torch-lit
      niches and ossified columns, Ori arrived at a vine-clad archway inscribed with
      curling sigils. The mirror glowed warm in her hand. Heart pounding, she pressed
      its face to the ancient stone. The vines parted as if paying homage, and the
      arch swung open on unseen hinges.\r\nBeyond lay a secret gallery of polished
      marble and iridescent tiles. Holographic murals shimmered on the walls\u2014ghostly
      reenactments of long-vanished feasts under constellations that no living soul
      remembered. Ori lifted her staff and traced the silver lines of an etched tableau:
      dancers swirling beneath radiant moons, priests raising chalices of starwater,
      scholars poring over scrolls in vaulted halls. The mirror-crown absorbed each
      scene, then projected it into living color above Ori\u2019s head, animating
      the silent hall in flickering light.\r\nAs the final vision faded, Ori realized
      she held more than a party trick. The gallery\u2019s secrets were no mere entertainment.
      They were fragments of her mountain\u2019s own memory, stored in pigment and
      tesserae, waiting for someone to awaken them. With her Mirror-Staff, she could
      reveal hidden glyphs, restore lost texts, and shed light on traditions buried
      beneath centuries of dust.\r\nWord spread among Olympus\u2019s craftsmen: Ori
      became both curator and storyteller. She led apprentices through the Echo Gate,
      teaching them to use the Mirror-Staff to read walls as one would read a book.
      And in her workshop, the air thrummed with renewed purpose as every shard of
      broken reflection, once thought worthless, found its place in the living mosaic
      of Olympus\u2019s forgotten past.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 58e5adca8af16ff4ea2f69284feb4210, type: 3}
    title: The Floating Archive
    description: "Suspended beneath a vast dome of starlight filaments, the Floating
      Archive hovered above Olympus\u2019s eastern terrace. Countless tomes\u2014bound
      in dragonhide-soft vellum and inscribed in metallic inks\u2014drifted gently
      among softly glowing runes. Archivist Vega, clad in robes spun from night-silk,
      spent her days cataloging volumes of cosmic lore: celestial maps of drifting
      star-dust, pulse-fractals charting ancient winds, and lullabies once sung to
      calm storm-tossed airships. Yet one peculiar scroll eluded her mastery\u2014its
      glyphs shimmered in and out of focus, never settling.\r\nCompelled to understand
      its secret, Vega followed the scroll\u2019s erratic glow into a concealed spiral
      staircase of polished alabaster. At its base stood a sentinel carved from comet
      glass, eyes dark as void and frame etched with gears that hummed like distant
      nebulae. The scroll pulsed once against the floor, and the sentinel\u2019s
      mirrorsplit gaze flickered in recognition. With a soft click, hidden gears
      turned, and the arched doors to the archive\u2019s inner sanctum swung open.\r\nInside,
      shelves heavy with dust-laden volumes rotated and descended in luminous arcs.
      Books floated free, their covers unfurling as if awakening from a long slumber.
      Vega watched, breath caught, as each tome whispered its tale: epics of solar
      storm-riders battling thunder dragons; lullabies that soothed sleeping moons;
      philosophical treatises penned by wandering comets debating the nature of time
      itself.\r\nDetermined to share this living library, Vega illuminated every
      chamber with crystals that refracted the tomes\u2019 ghostly projections onto
      the walls. Scholars, poets, and dreamers were invited to wander the aisles
      of floating lore. They sat in hushed reverence as verses drifted overhead,
      exchanging fragments of knowledge like gifts. The sentinel, once passive, hummed
      in harmony with their voices, becoming both guardian and collaborator in the
      archive\u2019s chorus.\r\nUnder Vega\u2019s guidance, the Floating Archive
      transformed from a repository of static scrolls into a dynamic nexus of living
      memory. Each visitor left with new questions and a thirst for discovery, while
      the archive\u2019s volumes\u2014once bound by silence\u2014sang with renewed
      resonance. And each night, Vega would drift among them, guiding the wandering
      pages through the starlight filaments, ensuring that every story\u2014no matter
      how long forgotten\u2014found its moment to shine.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7037136992f007b44b9cf07af9376dc6, type: 3}
    title: "Lyra\u2019s Phantom Pulse"
    description: "In the twilight hush of Olympus\u2019s northern cliff, Lyra explored
      an abandoned temple whose cracked marble corridors whispered of bygone ceremonies.
      Sunlight filtered through collapsed archways, illuminating motes of dust that
      danced like suspended stars. Yet beneath the ruins\u2019 stillness, Lyra\u2019s
      holo-lens detected a faint, rhythmic thump\u2014a phantom heartbeat echoing
      through fractured floors.\r\nEntranced, she cleared rubble from a sunken dais
      to reveal an ancient heart-drum carved from petrified starlight. Deep grooves
      circled its base, etched with symbols of breath and time. Kneeling, Lyra placed
      her palm on the drum\u2019s surface. A gentle shiver coursed through her arm
      as though the drum recognized a kindred pulse. Summoning courage, she tapped
      one soft cadence\u2014tap\u2026pause\u2026tap\u2014and the ruin responded.\r\nMarble
      pillars quivered in low hums. Vines trembled, releasing petals that twirled
      like glowing fireflies. Motes of airborne crystal refracted her tapping into
      arcs of light. Lyra\u2019s simple rhythm wove itself into the temple\u2019s
      own forgotten song, awakening currents that had lain dormant since the mountain\u2019s
      forging.\r\nWord of the Phantom Pulse spread quickly. Pilgrims climbed the
      steep trails to stand at the dais, adding their own rhythms\u2014gentle taps
      from children\u2019s fingers, the confident beats of seasoned drummers, even
      the hush of a scholar\u2019s pen as it scribbled notes in the margins of her
      journal. Each heartbeat layered onto the drum\u2019s ancient mantra, transforming
      the ruin into a living chorus of hearts.\r\nLyra, once solitary in her quest,
      found herself at the heart of a community bound by shared pulse. Travelers
      arrived at dawn\u2019s first light, bringers of rhythms and souls in search
      of harmony. Archaeologists paused their brushes to join the ritual; musicians
      composed ballads whose choruses echoed the temple\u2019s resonant hum. And
      every night, under the glow of twin moons, Lyra returned to the dais. Palm
      to drum, she listened as the Phantom Pulse merged heartbeats across generations\u2014reminding
      Olympus that no heartbeat is too faint to awaken the stones beneath one\u2019s
      feet.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e99baaac8b9060e4fa6e7587f796a822, type: 3}
    title: The Radiant Pillar of Dawn
    description: "On the rolling heath just below Olympus\u2019s summit rose the
      Radiant Pillar\u2014a towering column of trapped sunrise, its crystalline core
      refracting every hue of dawn. Legends warned that any who attempted to harness
      its brilliance would unleash blinding storms across the plateau. Yet seeker
      Arin, lantern in hand and resolve in heart, braved the chill of pre-dawn mists
      to uncover the pillar\u2019s secret.\r\nHis lantern flickered out as he approached,
      leaving only the pillar\u2019s warm glow to light his path. Arin circled its
      base, tracing etched runes that pulsed softly beneath his fingertips. With
      a steady breath, he pressed his palm against the crystal facets. A wave of
      gentle warmth flooded through him, aligning his pulse to the pillar\u2019s
      own rhythmic thrum. The runes blazed in concentric rings as light rippled outward
      like morning rays across dark waters.\r\nFar across the heath, hidden springs
      of luminescent moss awoke. Their tendrils stretched toward the pillar\u2019s
      glow, unfurling in radiant arcs. Pools at its base glowed sapphire and rose,
      reflecting the dawn sky as if in tribute. Nearby, dunes of silver sand shifted,
      revealing ancient mosaic tiles that had lain buried for centuries\u2014patterns
      depicting travelers guided by a pillar\u2019s light.\r\nWord spread that the
      Radiant Pillar offered safe passage through the plateau\u2019s treacherous
      fogs. Caravans once lost in swirling mists now followed its glow, camping in
      its warm radiance at twilight. Farmers built markers of polished quartz in
      its shadow, lighting lanterns each dawn in gratitude. Artists flocked to capture
      its shifting spectrum on canvas, while poets composed ballads celebrating its
      steadfast beacon.\r\nArin, once a lone seeker, became keeper of the Dawnlight.
      Each morning he stood beside the pillar, lantern in one hand and a cup of steaming
      tea in the other, welcoming travelers with a quiet smile. In the hush before
      sunrise, he placed his hand on the crystal and felt the plateau stir beneath
      his touch. And as the first rays broke the horizon, Arin knew that even in
      the coldest heights of Olympus, a single spark of radiance can carve a path
      of warmth and hope for all who follow its glow.\r\n"
